<title>BELGIUM: Commission seeks detail on French betting tax.</title>
<headline>Commission seeks detail on French betting tax.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had asked France for clarification of measures it had taken affecting bets on horse races.</p>
<p>The measures concern a decrease of 1.1 percent on the taxation of such bets, to the benefit of the Societe des Courses, to finance France's so-called PMU and PMH social plans, the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Commission said it needed the information in order to determine whether the measures amounted to state aid. If it did, Commission would have to see whether it broke the EU's single market rules.</p>
<p>Commission investigations come after complaints from British bookmakers Ladbrokes.</p>
</text>
